Return decrypted Schannel data without waiting to fill the buffer.
tls_read kept reading from the socket until the caller's buffer was
full or the peer closed the connection. The TLS copy loop passes a
64 KiB buffer, so a short reply stayed unread until 64 KiB had arrived
or the server hung up. Request-response protocols stalled: wget over
ftps never got past the server's greeting, and an https download only
finished when the server closed the connection. Once some data has been
decrypted, return it instead of blocking for the next record.

---
 networking/tls.c |    8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/networking/tls.c
+++ b/networking/tls.c
@@ -3330,7 +3330,13 @@
 					goto Success;
 				}
 				case SEC_E_INCOMPLETE_MESSAGE: {
-					int result = safe_read(state->ifd,
+					int result;
+
+					/* Return what we have rather than block for more */
+					if (amount_read > 0)
+						goto Success;
+
+					result = safe_read(state->ifd,
 						state->in_buffer + state->in_buffer_offset,
 						sizeof(state->in_buffer) - state->in_buffer_offset);
 					if (result == 0) {
